A||N||3||Monkeyman||Isuzu Rodeo Sport (formerly Amigo)||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-23-2001||04:51 AM||||Anyone own one?  My wife and I are planning an SUV (there, I said the bad word  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) purchase in the next year or so.  We want a 2 door and the only new 2 door we can afford is this.  We're also considering used Blazers (both full size and mini) and possibly used Ford Explorers (without Firestone tires, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>All I really know (from Isuzus' website) is that I can get a fully loaded 4x4 with a semi soft top, V6/auto (wife can't drive a stick) for around 16 grand.  I know that the warranty is outstanding (something like 10/100k?).  Would this mean that the quality is up to that, or is this just a selling gimmick?  I don't want something that will end up in the shop every month no matter who foots the bill as the nearest Isuzu dealer is about 45 miles away.<P>Are there other good (used) SUVs out there that I'm not thinking of?  I'm obviously staying away from the high end SUVs (M-B, Lexus, Toyota, etc) for cost reasons even though they may be more reliable.  I would prefer full size, but my wife prefers small so either would work.<P>Any help would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||10-23-2001||07:44 AM||||i got my wife a "97 Honda Passport last winter (they are the same as the Rodeo's).  they are solid and reliable cars.<P>are you talking about buying her a new vehicle, or a used one?  if yo want used, i would suggest you try to find a way into the dealer auction.  you get much better prices that way.  <P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||10-23-2001||07:58 AM||||My father owned an Isuzu truck a few years ago.  Had nothing but good things to say about it.  Not nearly as refined as say a Toyota or Nissan, but reliable as all get out and a decent-looking vehicle too.<P>If "used" is an option, I'd recommend a 3-5 year old Toyota 4Runner or Nissan Pathfinder.  I've got a '94 Pathfinder with 110,000 miles on it and I could gab all day about how much I love this truck!  I highly recommend one!||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||10-23-2001||09:13 AM||||If you are like 99.9% of small SUV owners and are not planning on heavy off-road use, I'd check out the Hyundai Santa Fe. 100,000 mi powertrain warranty. I was looking at the XG300L, it looks like the Koreans are putting out much much better stuff nowadays. Of course the Santa Fe is a 4 door, but take it from a sister in law of mine that just bought a 2 door Jimmy, 4 doors are much more convenient and you'll wind up wishing you'd chose differently.||||reg||1
